 price embeds a success probability far above base rates. My bull case\n(25% weight) already assumes sustained mid-teens revenue growth for a decade \u2014\nabove the 40% base rate for quality compounders sustaining >8% FCF CAGR. Three\ncompany-specific justifications for a bullish deviation:\n1. Q2 2026 Fitness +41% YoY with GM 62.4% \u2014 an accelerating product cycle with\n   reported evidence, not a TAM narrative [Actual \u2014 Garmin IR; marineindustrynews]\n2. Aviation AXIS platform: a new, scalable cockpit-display product family aimed at\n   a large certified retrofit market \u2014 a genuine second S-curve [Actual \u2014 Q2 release]\n3. Vertical integration + 60% GM + net cash: competitive position is stronger than\n   the average wearables hardware vendor\n\nStep 1.5-3. Base Rate Shock Check:\nSuccess probability implied by price \u2248 60\u201370% (required to justify 29x forward),\nvs base rate ~40% \u2192 deviation >1.5x base rate \u2192 ADDITIONAL EVIDENCE REQUIRED.\nThe evidence available (two quarters of beat-and-raise) is necessary but not\nsufficient. This is a RED FLAG for valuation prudence.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY (BUFFETT + LYNCH)\n\nStep 2-1. Business Understanding (3 sentences):\nGarmin designs and manufactures GPS-enabled devices and services across five\nsegments: Fitness wearables & coaching software, Outdoor adventure watches &\nsatellite communicators, Aviation cockpit avionics, Marine electronics, and Auto\nOEM cockpit platforms. It is vertically integrated (design, manufacturing,\ndistribution) and generated $7.246B revenue and $1.664B net income in FY2025.\nRecent acquisitions (TrainingPeaks, TrainHeroic) shift the Fitness segment toward\nsubscription-based coaching/software.\nUnderstandability: HIGH.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat Assessment (0\u20133 per type, total /21):\n\u2022 Intangible assets/brand: 3 \u2014 category-defining brand; premium pricing holds\n\u2022 Switching costs: 2 \u2014 Connect ecosystem, TrainingPeaks lock-in; voluntary upgrade cycles\n\u2022 Network effects: 1.5 \u2014 Connect community real but modest\n\u2022 Cost advantage: 2 \u2014 vertical integration; Taiwan manufacturing scale\n\u2022 Economies of scale: 2 \u2014 R&D amortized across 5 segments; 60% GM at $7B+ scale\n\u2022 Regulatory barriers: 2 \u2014 FAA/STC certification in aviation, marine standards\n\u2022 Data moat: 1.5 \u2014 130M+ connected devices; not yet monetized at scale\nTOTAL: 14/21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT.\nMoat direction: WIDENING (Fitness via software/subscriptions; Aviation via AXIS);\nSTABLE (Outdoor, Marine); NARROWING (Auto OEM \u2014 OEMs control terms; Q2 OM on Auto\nOEM was $3M/$172M = 1.7%).\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch Classification: FAST GROWER with quality characteristics.\nCheckpoints: revenue CAGR 11.6% (5-yr); EPS growth 19.4% CAGR; net cash; ROE 22%.\nThe classic fast-grower warning (PEG >2) applies: forward PEG = 29.2 / 8.7 \u2248 3.4.\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard:\n\u2022 Revenue 3-yr CAGR: 14.2% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Operating margin: 25.9% (FY2025); 12-yr median 23.6% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Diluted EPS CAGR (FY2022\u2192FY2025): 19.4% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 ROE: 21.9% [Actual \u2014 vendor consensus]; Adjusted ROIC ~32% [Estimate]\n\u2022 FCF margin: 18.8% (FY2025 reported); FCF/NI conversion: 82% [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Net debt: NET CASH $3.774B (cash+ST+LT investments $4.135B \u2212 LT debt $0.165B\n  \u2212 operating leases $0.196B) [Arithmetic/Estimate]\n\u2022 Interest coverage: >200x (OI $1.876B vs ~$8M interest on $0.165B) [Estimate]\nJUDGMENT: EXCELLENT.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard (0\u20133 each; bonus):\n1. Buyback efficiency: 2 \u2014 $500M authorized 2026-02-13 through 2028-12-30 [Actual \u2014\n   investors.garmin.com]; Q2 2026 buyback only $43M; 3-yr net issuance \u22120.0% [Arithmetic].\n   Disciplined at rich prices; not aggressive.\n2. M&A track record: 2 \u2014 bolt-on history; TrainingPeaks/TrainHeroic strategically\n   sound; price undisclosed [Unconfirmed]; no large impairments historically [Estimate]\n3. Capex efficiency: 3 \u2014 $270M capex on $1.66B NI; incremental ROIC >> WACC\n4. Rationality of mix: 3 \u2014 dividend +17% to $4.20/sh; buyback authorized; low capex;\n   bolt-on M&A\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3 \u2014 beat-and-raise twice in 2026; consistent record\nTOTAL: 13/15. Insider ownership 14.69% \u2192 +1. Insider 6-mo net buy: [Unconfirmed].\nADJUSTED: 14/16.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\nStep 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization: R&D is not broken out in the pack [Unconfirmed];\ntypical Garmin R&D \u2248 10% of revenue (~$725M FY2025) [Estimate]. Capitalizing at\n4-yr straight-line: adjusted OI uplift \u2248 R&D \u2212 amort \u2248 +$180M/yr at maturity.\nAdjusted ROIC = (NOPAT $1.72B) / (equity $8.973B + debt $0.361B + unamortized R&D\n~$2.2B \u2212 cash $4.135B = $7.4B) \u2248 23% vs GAAP ROIC ~20% \u2014 +3pt uplift.\n\nStep 2.5-2. SBC Treatment: SBC was $166M (FY2025), 2.3% of revenue, and is already\nan operating expense within reported operating income. The DCF in this report\ntherefore treats SBC as a real cash-equivalent expense (it is NOT added back).\nThis matches the pack instruction that OCF-based owner earnings must subtract SBC.\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization: added $0.196B to debt; adjusted net\ncash = $3.774B. Note: operating-lease column is [Estimate] for the lease liability;\nan error of \u00b1$0.2B shifts IV by ~\u00b1$1/share.\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/Data Asset: brand is strong but not separately valued; data asset\n(health/fitness data from ~130M+ devices) is unmonetized \u2014 the market's platform\npremium, if any, sits entirely in the bull case [Unconfirmed, not quantified].\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (FY2025): NI $1.664B + D&A $0.185B \u2212 maintenance capex\n~$0.149B (\u224855% of $0.270B) [Assumption] \u2212 \u0394Operating WC ~$0.38B [Estimate]\n= $1.32B. This validates the model FCF method (model FY2025: ~$1.20\u20131.36B).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1: TRADITIONAL DCF + MULTIPLES\n\nStep 3-0. Forecast Drivers and Sources:\n\n(a) REVENUE:\n\u2022 FY2025: $7.246B [Actual]\n\u2022 FY2026E: $8.05B \u2014 COMPANY GUIDANCE, raised 2026-07-29 [Actual \u2014 IBD/Garmin IR]\n\u2022 2027E: +10.0% [Assumption \u2014 above consensus fade; Fitness +17%, Aviation +12%\n  offset Auto flat]\n\u2022 2028E: +9.0%; 2029E: +8.0%; 2030E: +7.0%; 2031E: +7.0%; 2032E: +6.0%;\n  2033E: +6.0%; 2034E: +5.0%; 2035E: +5.0% [Assumption \u2014 glide path; post-2026\n  guidance does not exist and is NOT established by any company source; shown\n  explicitly rather than silently extrapolated]\n\u2022 Implied 2026\u201335 revenue CAGR: ~7.0%. For contrast, the 5-yr trailing CAGR is\n  11.6% [Arithmetic].\n\nSegment bridge (FY2025 base [Estimate]; sums to $7.246B):\n| Segment | FY2025E | FY2026E | YoY | 2035E | CAGR 26\u201335 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Fitness | $2.14B | $2.57B | +20% | $5.40B | ~8.6% |\n| Outdoor | $1.95B | $2.12B | +9% | $3.20B | ~4.7% |\n| Aviation | $1.24B | $1.39B | +12% | $2.80B | ~8.1% |\n| Marine | $1.07B | $1.17B | +9% | $1.80B | ~4.9% |\n| Auto OEM | $0.85B | $0.80B | \u22125% | $1.35B | ~6.0% |\n| Other/software overlay | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | $0.23B | \u2014 |\n| TOTAL | $7.25B | $8.05B | +11.1% | $14.78B | 7.0% |\nFY2026E segment growth calibrated to Q2 2026 reported: Fitness +41%, Outdoor +11%,\nAuto +1% [Actual \u2014 marineindustrynews/investing.com]; full-year Fitness tempering\n(+20%) is my deliberate choice because Q2 was flattered by new-product launches.\nAuto OEM decline in 2026 reflects the delayed Mercedes ramp to 2027 [Estimate \u2014\nGlobe and Mail Q1 transcript].\n\n(b) OPERATING MARGIN:\n\u2022 2026E: 27.0% = COMPANY GUIDED full-year OM [Actual \u2014 IBD/Garmin slides]\n\u2022 2027E: 27.3%; 2028E: 27.8%; 2029E: 28.2%; 2030E: 28.4%; 2031\u201335E: 28.5%\n  [Assumption \u2014 gradual mix drift toward software/premium; Q2 2026 was 30.4% incl.\n  a $21M tariff refund; my glide is deliberately below the Q2 print to avoid\n  over-extrapolating a one-off quarter]\n\n(c) CAPEX: 3.5% of revenue [Estimate \u2014 FY2025 actual 3.7%; TTM capex $0.297B on\n$7.464B revenue; no long-dated capex plan disclosed [Unconfirmed]]\n\n(d) D&A: 2.5% of revenue [Assumption \u2014 FY2025 actual 2.6%]\n\n(e) WORKING CAPITAL: \u0394WC = 23% of incremental revenue [Estimate \u2014 operating WC\nex-cash/revenue: 22.7% (2023), 21.1% (2024), 24.7% (2025); average 22.8%]\n\n(f) TAX: 16.5% (2026) \u2014 COMPANY GUIDED [Actual \u2014 Garmin IR via Finansavisen: Q2\neffective tax 16.8%, prior-year 16.5%; the company guided 16.5% for FY2026].\n2027\u20132030: 16.5%; 2031\u20132035: 17.0% [Assumption \u2014 reversal risk]\n\n(g) DISCOUNT RATE (WACC):\n\u2022 Rf: 4.71% (10Y, Aug 21 2026) [Actual]\n\u2022 ERP: 4.5% [Assumption \u2014 standard post-2020 range 4.3\u20134.8%]\n\u2022 Beta: 0.874 vendor [Actual], adjusted to 0.90 [Assumption] to reflect consumer\n  durable cyclicality\n\u2022 Cost of equity: 4.71% + 0.90\u00d74.5% = 8.76% \u2192 8.7%\n\u2022 After-tax cost of debt: ~4.0% (0.3% weight) [Estimate]\n\u2022 WACC: 8.7% (equity 99.7%, debt 0.3%)\n\n(h) TERMINAL GROWTH: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 nominal GDP ceiling ~4\u20134.5%; 3.0% is\nconservative for a durable compounder; sensitivity 2.5\u20133.5% shown]\n\nStep 3-1. Explicit DCF ($B):\n| FY | Rev | OM% | OI | Tax% | NOPAT | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | FCFF | PV@8.7% |\n|----|-----|-----|-----|------|-------|-----|-------|-----|------|--------|\n| 2026 | 8.050 | 27.0 | 2.174 | 16.5 | 1.815 | 0.201 | 0.282 | 0.185 | 1.549 | 1.425 |\n| 2027 | 8.850 | 27.3 | 2.416 | 16.5 | 2.017 | 0.221 | 0.310 | 0.184 | 1.744 | 1.476 |\n| 2028 | 9.650 | 27.8 | 2.683 | 16.5 | 2.240 | 0.241 | 0.338 | 0.184 | 1.959 | 1.525 |\n| 2029 | 10.420 | 28.2 | 2.938 | 16.5 | 2.453 | 0.261 | 0.365 | 0.177 | 2.172 | 1.556 |\n| 2030 | 11.150 | 28.4 | 3.167 | 16.5 | 2.644 | 0.279 | 0.390 | 0.168 | 2.365 | 1.558 |\n| 2031 | 11.930 | 28.5 | 3.400 | 17.0 | 2.822 | 0.298 | 0.418 | 0.179 | 2.523 | 1.529 |\n| 2032 | 12.640 | 28.5 | 3.602 | 17.0 | 2.990 | 0.316 | 0.442 | 0.163 | 2.701 | 1.506 |\n| 2033 | 13.400 | 28.5 | 3.819 | 17.0 | 3.170 | 0.335 | 0.469 | 0.175 | 2.861 | 1.468 |\n| 2034 | 14.070 | 28.5 | 4.010 | 17.0 | 3.328 | 0.352 | 0.492 | 0.154 | 3.034 | 1.432 |\n| 2035 | 14.780 | 28.5 | 4.212 | 17.0 | 3.496 | 0.370 | 0.517 | 0.163 | 3.186 | 1.383 |\n\n\u03a3 PV(FCFF 2026\u20132035) = $14.86B\nTerminal value = 3.186 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.087 \u2212 0.03) = $57.58B; PV = $25.00B\nEV operating = $39.86B\nNet cash = $4.135B \u2212 $0.165B \u2212 $0.196B = $3.774B\nEquity value = $43.63B\nPer share (193.6M diluted) = $225.40 \u2192 **BASE IV: $225**\n(Unadjusted for ~0.3%/yr share-count creep [Arithmetic]; $225 \u2248 $222 with the drag.)\n\nStep 3-2. Reverse DCF (what $292.26 implies):\nEquity $56.36B \u2192 EV $52.59B. At WACC 8.7%, g 3.0%, the market requires either:\n(a) ~9.5% FCFF CAGR for a decade (\u2248 the BULL case) or\n(b) base-case cash flows at a 7.6% WACC (i.e., a ~110bp rate decline).\nVerdict: FEASIBLE BUT DEMANDING \u2014 the price does not embed a margin of safety.\n\nStep 3-3. Multiples Cross-Check:\n\u2022 Forward P/E: 29.2x vs Garmin 5-yr average ~22x [Estimate] \u2192 33% premium\n\u2022 EV/EBITDA: $52.59B / ($2.174B OI + $0.201B D&A) = 22.1x [Estimate]\n\u2022 P/FCF: $56.36B / $1.68B = 33.6x [Estimate]\n\u2022 PEG: 3.4 (on 8.7% consensus EPS growth) [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 Dividend yield: $4.20/$292.26 = 1.44% [Estimate]\nAll four multiples sit above both history and quality-compounder norms.\n\nStep 3-4. Tornado Sensitivity (Top 3 variables):\n\u2022 WACC (8.0% \u2192 $260; 9.5% \u2192 $195) \u2014 most sensitive\n\u2022 Revenue CAGR post-2026 (\u00b11pt \u2192 \u00b1$25\u201330)\n\u2022 OM trajectory (\u00b1150bps \u2192 \u00b1$22)\nMinor: terminal g (2.5% \u2192 $215; 3.5% \u2192 $239); tax (19% \u2192 ~$216).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n\u2022 Competitive response (Apple): \u22122. If Garmin maintains >20% Fitness growth, Apple\n  is incentivized to ship a multi-day-battery rugged watch. A 7-day Apple Watch\n  would erode Garmin's core functional moat.\n\u2022 Reflexivity: +1. High stock price funds SBC-based talent ($166M) and M&A currency;\n  consumer brand perception benefits.\n\u2022 Customer evolution: +1. Fitness buyers moving from early-adopter to mainstream;\n  TrainingPeaks/CIRQA lift subscription attach, raising LTV; churn is low.\n\u2022 Net second-order impact: 0 (neutral).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\nPrior: Quality compounder sustaining >8% FCF growth for a decade \u2014 ~40% [Estimate].\nLikelihood from Q2 2026 evidence (record quarter, fitness +41%, guidance raised\ntwice) \u2192 adjusts the posterior to:\n\u2022 BEAR (25%): Fitness decelerates to <10% by 2028; Auto OEM stays ~flat at low\n  margin; OM compresses to 24%; terminal g 2.5% \u2192 IV $151\n\u2022 BASE (50%): Per Section 3 DCF \u2192 IV $225\n\u2022 BULL (25%): Fitness sustains >20% through 2028; Aviation AXIS + Auto OEM ramp;\n  OM 30%; terminal g 3.5% \u2192 IV $285\nProbabilities total 100%. Base case is the modal outcome.\n\nExpected price = 0.25\u00d7151 + 0.50\u00d7225 + 0.25\u00d7285 = **$220**\n50% CI: $151\u2013$285 | 80% CI: ~$145\u2013$303 [Estimate]\nMargin of safety: Base \u221229.9% (None) | Expected-value basis \u221232.8% (None)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2