ng earnings, worst-case \u221250% or more [Estimate].\n\u2022 Common bear trigger with other long-duration consumer/quality positions: a Fed\n  HIKE (currently ~1/3 odds) is the single largest cluster risk.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY + PRE-MORTEM)\n\nThesis KPIs (trigger levels):\n1. Fitness quarterly growth: <10% YoY for two consecutive quarters \u2192 downgrade to\n   Bear thesis (saturation/competitive attack).\n2. Consolidated GM (ex-tariff refunds): <58% for two quarters \u2192 margin thesis broken.\n3. Auto OEM quarterly revenue: <$150M or OM <0 \u2192 auto is a value-destroying\n   distraction; cap auto at 10% of FY model.\n4. Subscriber counts/ARR for TrainingPeaks + Garmin Connect paid tiers [Unconfirmed \u2014\n   company does not disclose; request disclosure in IR]; if attach rate <5% of\n   installed base by FY2028, kill the platform premium in the valuation.\n5. Buyback execution: >$250M of the $500M authorization completed ABOVE $250 \u2192\n   negative capital-allocation signal; completed BELOW $230 \u2192 positive.\n6. Macro trigger: 10Y >5.25% \u2192 WACC 9.0%+, revalue to ~$200; Fed cut cycle begins\n   \u2192 WACC 8.0%\u2212, revalue toward $260.\n\nPre-mortem: \"Today is 2031; GRMN failed. Why?\"\n(a) Fitness saturated \u2014 Apple shipped a 7-day battery watch in 2027 and Garmin\n    growth fell to 3%; (b) Auto OEM won $1.5B of revenue at 5% OM and dragged\n    consolidated OM below 23%; (c) the 2026 multiple of 29x compressed to 18x as\n    growth normalized, and the