tem monetization)\nValuation Engine: Engine 3 \u2014 Hybrid Valuation (Core Hardware Anchor + Platform Premium), cross-checked with Engine 1 DCF\n\nReason Engine 3 selected:\n1. GRMN derives the majority of revenue from device hardware (Fitness, Outdoor, Aviation, Marine, Auto OEM) [Actual \u2014 FY2025 revenue $7.246B, gross profit $4.256B].\n2. Recurring/platform revenue exists (inReach subscriptions, Pilot services, TrainingPeaks/TrainHeroic acquired in Q2 2026) but is not separately disclosed in the SEC pack [Unconfirmed \u2014 segment/service mix not disclosed].\n3. Gross margin 60.6% FY2025 / 62.4% Q2 2026 is hardware+software blended and cannot be modeled as a pure software business [Actual \u2014 press release].\n4. The company is not a pure option-led story: FY2025 FCF was $1.363B, OCF $1.633B, and guidance is concrete [Actual \u2014 SEC data]. Engine 4 (pure optionality) is inappropriate.\n5. Using Engine 1 alone (pure DCF on consolidated FCF) is the correct starting point, but it under-weights the optionality in TrainingPeaks, CIRQA, aviation software, and Auto OEM domain controllers. Engine 3 explicitly adds a platform premium.\n\nTransition assessment: GRMN is in early transition from Product-Platform Hybrid toward Quality Compounder. Criteria status:\n- ROIC > WACC for 3 consecutive years: yes [Estimate \u2014 ROIC ~30% vs WACC 9%]\n- Installed-base monetization established at scale: only early stage [Assumption]\n- Recurring revenue > 50% of total: no\nBecause only 50-80% of transition criteria are met, the company is treated as a blended Engine 3, with a 0.5-step conviction discount applied for transition uncertainty.\n\nModel confidence: MODERATE. The SEC-sourced pack is reliable, but segment detail is absent, post-2026 guidance is absent, and long-run revenue growth is Tier 4 estimation-heavy.\n\nExpected output summary:\n- Analyst\u2019s point intrinsic value: $185/share [Estimate]\n- Scenario expected value: $182/share [Estimate]\n- Margin of safety vs $292.26: -58% to -62%, i.e., NONE\n- Final action: REDUCE / DO NOT INITIATE\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 1-1. Macro variable check (all at T0)\n- 10-year U.S. Treasury yield: 4.74% [Actual \u2014 FRED/TradingEconomics, 2026-08-21], direction: stable-to-rising\n- Federal funds target: 3.50%\u20133.75%, unchanged at July 2026 FOMC [Actual \u2014 TradingEconomics]\n- Dollar index (DXY): 98.96 [Actual \u2014 TradingView, 2026-08-25], weak vs historical\n- Fed stance: Neutral/Easing bias, with market pricing a small chance of a hike [Estimate]\n- Global liquidity: mildly restrictive but stable [Assumption]\n- Economic cycle position: late expansion / early cooling [Assumption]\n- Inflation: not held in pack; policy data imply inflation is not yet fully normalized [Unconfirmed]\n- Credit spreads: not retrieved; not a primary driver for GRMN [Unconfirmed]\n\nStep 1-2. Regime probability distribution\n- Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 35%\n- Reflation (high rates + growth): 25%\n- Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 20%\n- Recession (low rates + low growth): 20%\nSum = 100% [Assumption \u2014 macro regime probabilities are inherently subjective]\n\nStep 1-3. Macro sensitivity matrix (scale -3 to +3)