25-35%), but TrainingPeaks/TrainHeroic are small, tuck-in acquisitions; base rate for small tuck-ins is higher, ~40-50% [Assumption]\n\n1.5-2. Deviation from base rate and company-specific justification\nThe market price implies GRMN will beat the platform-transition base rate. Company-specific justifications:\n1. 58 million+ lifetime installed devices and 20 million+ units shipped in FY2025 give a real base for service upsell (inReach, Garmin Pay, TrainingPeaks) [Actual \u2014 press release]\n2. Aviation segment has certification-based lock-in (75% gross margin, Best Supplier of the Year to Embraer for 11 straight years) [Actual \u2014 press release]\n3. Fitness segment grew 32% in H1 2026, while the global smartwatch market was roughly flat/declining; this demonstrates share capture not just market growth [Actual \u2014 press release; Estimate \u2014 IDC]\nThese justify some deviation upward, but not the full premium embedded in the current price.\n\n1.5-3. Base-rate shock check\nThe market-implied success path (2027-2035 revenue CAGR of ~10-15% at a 20%+ terminal FCF margin) is more than 2\u00d7 the base platform-transition success rate. RED FLAG triggered. Direct evidence of durable 10-year double-digit growth is not available from any company filing; therefore, the valuation is downgraded to below-market.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n2-1. Business understanding\nGarmin designs, manufactures, and sells GPS-enabled devices across Fitness, Outdoor, Aviation, Marine, and Auto OEM. It monetizes hardware with embedded software, and is slowly adding subscriptions/services (inReach, TrainingPeaks). Understandability: HIGH.\n\n2-2. Moat assessment\n| Moat type | Score (0-3) | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand, patents) | 3 | Widening |\n| Switching costs | 2 | Stable |\n| Network effects | 1 | Stable |\n| Cost advantage (vertical integration) | 3 | Stable |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening |\n| Regulatory barriers (aviation certification) | 2 | Stable |\n| Data moat | 2 | Widening |\n| TOTAL | 15/21 | WIDE MOAT, direction stable-to-widening |\n\n2-3. Lynch classification\nClassification: STALWART leaning FAST GROWER (Fitness/Outdoor growing double digits; Aviation/Marine steady; AutoOEM small).\nKey checkpoints:\n- Share gain: Fitness +32% H1 2026 vs market ~flat [Actual / Estimate]\n- Balance sheet strength: net cash ~$3.77-3.97B [Arithmetic \u2014 own calculation]\n- Product cycle risk: high, but broad segment diversification reduces it\n\n2-4. Financial strength scorecard\n- Revenue CAGR (FY2020-FY2025): 11.6% [Arithmetic \u2014 pack Section 7]\n- Revenue growth FY2025: +15.1% [Arithmetic \u2014 $7.246B / $6.297B]\n- Operating margin FY2025: 25.9% [Arithmetic]\n- TTM net income: $1.736B [Actual]\n- ROE (GAAP): 19.8% on average equity [Arithmetic \u2014 own estimate]\n- ROIC: ~30% before R&D capitalization [Estimate \u2014 own calculation]\n- FCF margin FY2025: 18.8% [Arithmetic \u2014 $1.363B / $7.246B]\n- FCF conversion: 83.5% of OCF [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt: negative (net cash) [Estimate \u2014 own calculation]\nJudgment: EXCELLENT\n\n2-5. Capital allocation scorecard\n- Buyback discipline: modest; $43M in Q2 2026, $448M remaining under $500M authorization through Dec 2028; not aggressive below valuation. Score: 1/3\n- M&A track record: tuck-ins logical (TrainingPeaks/TrainHeroic); no disclosed impairments. Score: 2/3\n- Capex efficiency: incremental ROIC far above WACC; but capex is rising due to Thailand expansion. Score: 2/3\n- Rationality of mix: balanced reinvestment + dividends + moderate buybacks. Score: 2/3\n- Guidance accuracy: raised FY2026 guidance after beating; record of conservative/beatable guidance. Score: 3/3\nBase capital allocation score: 10/15\nInsider bonuses: insider ownership 14.69% +1; no verified insider buying or selling cluster [Unconfirmed] \u2014 no further adjustment.\nTotal capital allocation score: 11/15\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n2.5-1. R&D capitalization\n- FY2025 R&D expense: $1.126B [Estimate \u2014 Macrotrends/Statista-derived; not in SEC pack]\n- Assume 4-year useful life, straight-line amortization [Assumption]\n- Approximate 4-year average R&D amortization: $0.98B [Estimate]\n- Adjusted operating income = $1.876B + $1.126B - $0.98B = $2.02B [Estimate]\n- Adjusted NOPAT at 16.5% tax = $1.69B [Estimate]\n\n2.5-2. SBC treatment\n- FY2025 SBC: $0.166B [Actual \u2014 SEC companyfacts]\n- Adjusted FCF = reported FCF $1.363B - SBC $0.166B = $1.197B [Arithmetic]\n- Share count is roughly flat (FY2025 diluted 193.616M), so dilution cost is modest.\n\n2.5-3. Operating lease capitalization\n- FY2025 operating leases: $0.196B [Actual]\n- Adjust net debt: gross cash+investments $4.135B - vendor debt $0.165B - operating leases $0.196B = net cash $3.774B [Arithmetic / Estimate]\n\n2.5-4. Brand/data asset estimation\nBrand asset: Garmin is a top-3 premium wearable brand and dominant in aviation/avionics; no reliable independent valuation retrieved. Data asset: health/fitness training data across a large installed base has real, but unquantified, monetization value. [Unconfirmed]\n\n2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC\n- Adjusted invested capital = reported invested capital ~$5.20B + unamortized R&D stock ~$3.4B = ~$8.6B [Estimate]\n- Adjusted ROIC = $1.69B / $8.6B = ~19.7% [Estimate]\n- GAAP ROIC is ~30%; gap >5pp is explained by R&D expensing. Conclusion: even adjusted, ROIC is more than 2\u00d7 WACC. Strong.\n\n2.5-6. Owner earnings (Buffett style)\n- Owner Earnings = Net income $1.664B + D&A $0.185B - maintenance capex (assumed $0.180B) - \u0394WC $0.700B = $0.969B [Estimate]\n- If we instead strip maintenance capex to ~$0.25B, Owner Earnings ~$0.90B. This is far below GAAP net income and explains the valuation gap.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3. VALUATION (ENGINE 3 + DCF CROSS-CHECK)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n3.1 Discount-rate derivation\n- Risk-free rate: 4.74% [Actual \u2014 10Y UST 2026-08-21]\n- Equity risk premium: 5.0% [Assumption]\n- Beta: 0.874 [Aggregator \u2014 vendor, unknown window; rounded to 0.90 for conservatism]\n- Cost of equity: 4.74% + 0.90 \u00d7 5.0% = 9.24% [Arithmetic / Assumption]\n- Company has negligible debt; WACC approximated at 9.0% [Assumption]\n\n3.2 Explicit forecast (base case, $B)\nFiscal years end late December. FY2026 revenue is company guidance [Actual]. All post-2026 numbers are [Assumption] because no company guidance exists beyond 2026 [Unconfirmed].\n\n| FY | Revenue | OM% | OI | Tax% | NOPAT | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | FCFF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2025A | 7.246 | 25.9% | 1.876 | 16.5% | 1.567 | 0.185 | 0.270 | 0.700 | 0.782 |\n| 2026E | 8.050 | 27.0% | 2.174 | 16.5% | 1.815 | 0.220 | 0.450 | 0.241 | 1.344 |\n| 2027E | 8.700 | 27.5% | 2.393 | 17.0% | 1.986 | 0.235 | 0.400 | 0.195 | 1.626 |\n| 2028E | 9.310 | 28.0% | 2.607 | 17.0% | 2.164 | 0.250 | 0.400 | 0.183 | 1.831 |\n| 2029E | 9.870 | 28.0% | 2.764 | 17.0% | 2.294 | 0.265 | 0.390 | 0.168 | 2.001 |\n| 2030E | 10.360 | 28.0% | 2.901 | 17.0% | 2.408 | 0.280 | 0.380 | 0.147 | 2.161 |\n| 2031E | 10.770 | 28.0% | 3.016 | 17.0% | 2.503 | 0.290 | 0.370 | 0.123 | 2.300 |\n| 2032E | 11.090 | 27.5% | 3.050 | 17.0% | 2.531 | 0.300 | 0.360 | 0.096 | 2.375 |\n| 2033E | 11.310 | 27.5% | 3.110 | 17.0% | 2.581 | 0.310 | 0.350 | 0.066 | 2.475 |\n| 2034E | 11.540 | 27.5% | 3.174 | 17.0% | 2.634 | 0.320 | 0.350 | 0.069 | 2.535 |\n| 2035E | 11.770 | 27.5% | 3.237 | 17.0% | 2.687 | 0.330 | 0.350 | 0.069 | 2.598 |\n\nForecast driver sources:\n- FY2026 revenue $8.05B, OM 27.0%, tax 16.5%: company raised guidance [Actual \u2014 Garmin press release 2026-07-29]\n- Revenue growth 2027-2029: 8%, 7%, 6%: [Assumption] \u2014 Q2 2026 segment growth was Fitness +25%, Marine +14%, Aviation +8%, Outdoor -2%, Auto OEM +1% [Actual]; global smartwatch unit market forecast roughly flat/declining 2026 per IDC [Estimate]; Garmin is taking share but cannot hold +11% consolidated growth indefinitely\n- Revenue growth 2030-2035: fading 5% to 2%: [Assumption]\n- OM beyond 2026: fades slightly after 2032 due to price competition and mix normalization [Assumption]\n- Capex 2026 $0.45B: [Estimate] \u2014 Q2 2026 implied capex of $128M (OCF $404M - FCF $276M [Actual]); full-year assumed at ~$0.45B due to Thailand capacity expansion\n- Capex 2027-2035: $0.35-0.40B [Assumption]\n- \u0394WC: 30% of incremental revenue [Assumption] \u2014 based on FY2025 actual \u0394WC of $0.700B vs revenue growth of $0.949B [Arithmetic]. This is conservative but appropriate given inventory increased to $1.772B in FY2025.\n\n3.3 DCF result\n- WACC = 9.0%, terminal growth = 2.0%\n- PV of explicit FCFF (FY2026-FY2035) = $13.0B\n- Terminal value = $2.598B \u00d7 1.02 / (0.09 - 0.02) = $37.9B\n- PV of terminal value = $15.99B\n- Enterprise value = $29.0B\n- + Net cash $3.77B = Equity value $32.8B\n- Per share = $32.8B / 192.853M = $170 [Estimate]\n\n3.4 Engine 3 core anchor stack cross-check\n- Forward EV/Sales (FY2026E): $52.6B / $8.05B = 6.5\u00d7 [Arithmetic]\n- Forward EV/Gross profit (FY2026E GP $4.806B): $52.6B / $4.806B = 10.9\u00d7 [Arithmetic]\n- Fair-value anchor stack (0.4 EV/Sales + 0.4 EV/GP + 0.2 peer):\n  - Assumed fair hardware/platform EV/Sales: 4.5\u00d7 [Assumption]\n  - Assumed fair EV/GP: 7.5\u00d7 [Assumption]\n  - Peer EV/Sales: 5.0\u00d7 [Assumption]\n  - Fair EV = 0.4\u00d7(4.5\u00d78.05) + 0.4\u00d7(7.5\u00d74.806) + 0.2\u00d7(5.0\u00d78.05) = $36.96B\n  - Add net cash $3.77B = $40.73B \u2192 $211/share [Estimate]\n\n3.5 Platform feature score\n- Installed base: 3/3 (300M+ lifetime products)\n- OTA/software updates: 2/3\n- Recurring monetization: 2/3 (inReach, Pilot services, TrainingPeaks)\n- Feedback loops/data: 2/3\n- Lock-in: 2/3 (strongest in aviation)\n- Platform score: 11/15 = 73%\nA modest platform premium of ~10% above hardware multiple is reasonable. Applying +10% to the anchor value gives ~$232/share [Assumption]. Since platform revenue is still a small fraction of total [Unconfirmed], the full premium is not justified. We apply a 50% haircut: fair platform-adjusted value \u2248 $220.\n\n3.6 Tornado sensitivity\nTop 3 variables:\n1. Long-run revenue CAGR (2026-2035): \u00b12pp changes IV by approximately \u00b1$35/share.\n2. Terminal operating margin: \u00b1200bp changes IV by approximately \u00b1$25/share.\n3. WACC: \u00b150bp changes IV by approximately \u00b1$20/share.\nThese three variables are the Thesis KPIs that must be monitored.\n\n3.7 Final base-case intrinsic value\nWeighted: 60% DCF ($170) + 40% Engine 3 anchor/platform ($220) = $190 [Estimate]\nScenario expected value (Section 4) = $182.\nFinal point IV used for margin of safety: $185.\n\nMargin of safety = ($185 - $292.26) / $185 = -58%.\nJudgment: NO margin of safety at $292.26.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n1. Competitive response: If Garmin continues taking share from Apple at the premium end, Apple will likely add more aggressive fitness/multisport features and price-promote Watch SE models. Impact on Garmin: -2 (moderate negative).\n2. Reflexivity: A rising stock price helps attract engineering talent and gives M&A currency (TrainingPeaks). A falling stock price could slow talent acquisition and weaken consumer brand perception, but less acute than for a capital-intensive company.\n3. Customer behavior evolution: Early adopters (runners, aviators, boaters) are already converted. Mainstream growth requires simpler devices like CIRQA; LTV/CAC may deteriorate as Garmin moves beyond its core athlete base.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nBayesian priors: informed by the base platform-transition rate (20-30%) plus Garmin\u2019s demonstrated execution. Posterior reflects the company-specific evidence above.\n\n| Scenario | Key assumptions | Probability | Intrinsic value | \n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | Wearables market matures; Apple and low-cost rivals erode pricing; Fitness growth falls to <5%; Outdoor declines; OM falls to 22%; revenue CAGR 3%; terminal g 1.5% | 30% | $120 |\n| Base | Garmin executes well; Fitness +8-10% through 2028, then mid-single-digit; Aviation/Marine grow high single-digit; OM stabilizes 27-28% | 45% | $185 |\n| Bull | Garmin becomes the default premium fitness ecosystem; TrainingPeaks/CIRQA unlock 10%+ recurring revenue; Fitness sustains 15%+; OM reaches 30%; revenue CAGR 10% | 25% | $260 |\n\nExpected value = 0.30\u00d7$120 + 0.45\u00d7$185 + 0.25\u00d7$260 = $182.\n50% CI: $130-$230 | 80% CI: $90-$300.\nThe current price of $292 is above the bull-case value, meaning the market is pricing in better-than-bull outcomes.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nMy investment horizon: 3-5 years.\nMarket-implied horizon: at 29\u00d7 forward EPS (FY2026E $10.00) and PEG ~3.8 trailing, the price appears to discount 10+ years of high single-to-low double-digit growth. Spread = negative 5-7 years. No horizon arbitrage exists; the market is looking further out than a disciplined investor should, without evidence of a 10-year secular growth runway.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\