licable \u2014 Garmin's M&A is bolt-on)\n\nStep 1.5-2. Deviation from Base Rate:\nThe market price embeds a success probability far above base rates. My bull case\n(25% weight) already assumes sustained mid-teens revenue growth for a decade \u2014\nabove the 40% base rate for quality compounders sustaining >8% FCF CAGR. Three\ncompany-specific justifications for a bullish deviation:\n1. Q2 2026 Fitness +41% YoY with GM 62.4% \u2014 an accelerating product cycle with\n   reported evidence, not a TAM narrative [Actual \u2014 Garmin IR; marineindustrynews]\n2. Aviation AXIS platform: a new, scalable cockpit-display product family aimed at\n   a large certified retrofit market \u2014 a genuine second S-curve [Actual \u2014 Q2 release]\n3. Vertical integration + 60% GM + net cash: competitive position is stronger than\n   the average wearables hardware vendor\n\nStep 1.5-3. Base Rate Shock Check:\nSuccess probability implied by price \u2248 60\u201370% (required to justify 29x forward),\nvs base rate ~40% \u2192 deviation >1.5x base rate \u2192 ADDITIONAL EVIDENCE REQUIRED.\nThe evidence available (two quarters of beat-and-raise) is necessary but not\nsufficient. This is a RED FLAG for valuation prudence.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY (BUFFETT + LYNCH)\n\nStep 2-1. Business Understanding (3 sentences):\nGarmin designs and manufactures GPS-enabled devices and services across five\nsegments: Fitness wearables & coaching software, Outdoor adventure watches &\nsatellite communicators, Aviation cockpit avionics, Marine