ized to ship a multi-day-battery rugged watch. A 7-day Apple Watch\n  would erode Garmin's core functional moat.\n\u2022 Reflexivity: +1. High stock price funds SBC-based talent ($166M) and M&A currency;\n  consumer brand perception benefits.\n\u2022 Customer evolution: +1. Fitness buyers moving from early-adopter to mainstream;\n  TrainingPeaks/CIRQA lift subscription attach, raising LTV; churn is low.\n\u2022 Net second-order impact: 0 (neutral).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\nPrior: Quality compounder sustaining >8% FCF growth for a decade \u2014 ~40% [Estimate].\nLikelihood from Q2 2026 evidence (record quarter, fitness +41%, guidance raised\ntwice) \u2192 adjusts the posterior to:\n\u2022 BEAR (25%): Fitness decelerates to <10% by 2028; Auto OEM stays ~flat at low\n  margin; OM compresses to 24%; terminal g 2.5% \u2192 IV $151\n\u2022 BASE (50%): Per Section 3 DCF \u2192 IV $225\n\u2022 BULL (25%): Fitness sustains >20% through 2028; Aviation AXIS + Auto OEM ramp;\n  OM 30%; terminal g 3.5% \u2192 IV $285\nProbabilities total 100%. Base case is the modal outcome.\n\nExpected price = 0.25\u00d7151 + 0.50\u00d7225 + 0.25\u00d7285 = **$220**\n50% CI: $151\u2013$285 | 80% CI: ~$145\u2013$303 [Estimate]\nMargin of safety: Base \u221229.9% (None) | Expected-value basis \u221232.8% (None)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nMarket-implied horizon: at 29.2x forward EPS, the market is paying for a decade of\nmid-teens growth (implied FCFF CAGR ~9.5%), i.e., a horizon well beyond 5 years.\nMy 3\u20135 year view (2029E):\n| Scenario | 2029E EPS | 2029E P/E | 2029E Price |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | $9.50 | 20x | $190 |\n| Base | $13.34 | 25x | $333 |\n| Bull | $16.50 | 30x | $495 |\nExpected 2029 price: 0.25\u00d7190 + 0.50\u00d7333 + 0.25\u00d7495 = $338 \u2192 +15.5% over 3 years \u2248\n+4.9% per year, versus an 8.7% cost of equity. Expected return is insufficient.\nHorizon arbitrage: NEGATIVE (the market's implied horizon exceeds my horizon and\npays below my hurdle).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\nConviction Score:\n1. Business quality: 4/5\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 1/5 (price is above bull-case IV)\n3. Macro alignment: 2/5\n4. Thesis clarity (KPIs): 4/5 (segment growth, GM, auto OEM, attach rates)\n5. Execution traceability: 4/5\nTotal: 15/25 \u2192 scaled to 15 = 9/15 \u2192 **CONVICTION: MEDIUM**\n\nConviction decay: \u22121 point per 6 months without confirming evidence (next review\nat FY2026 Q4 print, or earlier if price < $240).\nSizing cap for Medium conviction: 4\u20136% normal; macro headwind \u22121pt; no crow