SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nNo portfolio context was provided. Framework treatment:\n\u2022 GRMN's common bear triggers: US consumer spending downturn, Fed tightening beyond\n  current hold (hike risk), USD strength, business-aviation cycle downturn.\n\u2022 If the existing portfolio holds consumer-durable or large-cap tech, realize that\n  GRMN adds correlated risk rather than diversification.\n\u2022 If GRMN is already held, the correct action at $292 is to TRIM to \u22643% core weight\n  (tax-aware); every $10 above $285 is distribution, not accumulation.\n\u2022 GRMN makes sense as a long-term quality allocation only below $225 (base-case\n  MoS \u22650%).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\nOne-year horizon, scenario-expected intrinsic $220 plus dividend $6.30:\nExpected return = (220 + 6.30)/292.26 \u2212 1 = \u221222.6%.\nMarket expected return \u2248 +7% [Assumption].\nEdge = \u221222.6% \u2212 7% \u2248 \u221229.6%. Kelly fraction = edge/variance \u2248 NEGATIVE \u2192 0% weight.\nConsistency check (framework rule): Layer 5 sizing (0%) vs Layer 6.5 (0%) \u2014 gap 0%,\nno re-analysis required.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nCatalysts (12 months):\n1. 2027 BMW/Mercedes Auto OEM ramp \u2014 Mercedes delayed to 2027 [Estimate \u2014 Globe and\n   Mail Q1'26 transcript]; each $100M of auto OEM revenue at >5% OM adds ~$0.05 EPS\n2. AXIS aviation platform + aviation OEM backlogs \u2014 new certified-display TAM\n3. CIRQA screenless smart band and TrainingPeaks/TrainHeroic integration \u2014\n   subscription attach growth\n4. Continued fitness momentum: Q2 2026 +41%; beat-and-raise pattern\n5. Further buyback execution under the $500M authorization\n\nRisks:\n1. Valuation de-rating: 29x \u2192 22x = \u221225% even with delivered earnings\n2. Fitness competitive attack (Apple multi-day battery; Whoop/Oura subscription)\n3. Auto OEM margin dilution: $3M OI on $172M (1.7% OM) \u2014 not a business\n4. Tariff refund non-recurrence: Q2 GM 62.4% included $21M one-off [Actual \u2014 Q2\n   excerpt]; ex-refund GM ~61.3%\n5. Consumer spending sensitivity at 3.4% inflation with hike risk\n6. Insider selling at high prices [Unconfirmed]\n7. Inventory build: +$298M YoY (FY2025) \u2014 channel risk if demand falters\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\n\u2022 Tail correlation: GRMN (beta 0.874) will converge to market beta during stress;\n  its consumer-durable and aviation end-markets weaken precisely when equity markets\n  fall.\n\u2022 Conditional VaR estimate: in a 2022-style drawdown (rates up 150\u2013200bps, consumer\n  spending down), GRMN at 29x forward