below 23%; (c) the 2026 multiple of 29x compressed to 18x as\n    growth normalized, and the stock returned ~0% over 5 years despite good\n    operating performance.\nEach failure mode has a listed early indicator above.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\nStep 9-1. Short Thesis (7 bullets, same data):\n1. At 29.2x forward EPS, the price embeds a decade of ~9.5% FCF growth; the stock\n   is priced at my BULL-case intrinsic value, leaving zero room for error.\n2. Q2 2026's \"impressive\" 62.4% GM includes a $21M tariff refund; even ex-refund,\n   management itself guides FY26 GM to 59.7% \u2014 Q2 was a peak, not a run-rate.\n3. Auto OEM \"profitability\" is $3M on $172M (1.7% OM); Mercedes ramp is delayed to\n   2027; OEMs own the negotiating power. Auto OEM is a capital sink disguised as\n   optionality.\n4. Insider ownership is 14.69%, yet there is no disclosed insider buying at $290+\n   [Unconfirmed]; the $500M buyback is only 0.9% of market cap and Q2 execution\n   was a token $43M \u2014 insiders are not signaling $292 is cheap.\n5. The sell-side mean target ($290.29) sits BELOW the current price; the buyer of\n   GRMN at $292 has no analyst support left, only momentum.\n6. Garmin has de-rated after every product cycle: 2014\u201315 (28x \u2192 15x), 2021\u201322\n   (23x \u2192 15x). The current cycle is strong, but hardware cycles always normalize.\n7. Platform narrative is not yet numeric: TrainingPeaks is likely <$100M revenue\n   [Unconfirmed]; subscription is ~2\u20133% of sales. The market is paying 29x for\n   hardware earnings.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic Combat:\nLong logic strength: 7/10 (quality, execution, moat, growth all real).\nShort logic strength: 6/10 (valuation, cyclicality, auto dilution; but the short\nrelies on a growth deceleration that has not appeared).\nGap: ~1 point \u2192 CONVICTION STAYS MEDIUM (no further downgrade).\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial data: No Hindenburg/Culper-style report exists on file\n[Unconfirmed \u2014 not found in available briefs]. The research brief's claim of a 5%\noutdoor decline is CONTRADICTED by reported Q2 2026 Outdoor +11% [Actual \u2014 the\nfiling-derived press release outranks the brief]; treat the brief as unreliable\nwhere it conflicts with SECTIONS 3\u20136.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed Arguments (and revival conditions):\n\u2022 \"Apple will destroy Garmin\" \u2014 KILLED because 6 years of share gains contradict\n  it; REVIVED if Apple ships >7-day battery AND Garmin fitness <5% for 2 quarters.\n\u2022 \"Garmin has no recurring revenue\" \u2014 KILLED by TrainingPeaks/TrainHeroic/CIRQA;\n  REVIVED if subscription ARR <$50M by FY2028.\n\u2022 \"The stock is cheap on growth\" \u2014 KILLED: PEG 3.4 and P/FCF 33.6x are not cheap;\n  no revival conditions needed \u2014 it was never true.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\nA. Methodology: PASS \u2014 DCF + multiples + reverse DCF + scenario cross-check; no\n   single-method conclusion.\nB. Valuation: PASS \u2014 WACC 8.0/8.7/9.5%, g 2.5/3.0/3.5% sensitivities shown; IV\n   range $195\u2013$262; the conclusion 