ax 16.5%; terminal g 3.0%.\nRed-team concerns at entry: valuation (price > bull IV); auto OEM margin; fitness\nsustainability; insider non-buying.\nRe-evaluation triggers: price <$240; FY2026 Q4 print; fitness 2-quarter <10% growth;\n10Y >5.25% or start of Fed cuts; TrainingPeaks ARR disclosure.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\nACTION: AVOID new purchases at $292.26. For existing holders: REDUCE \u2014 trim to a\n\u22643% core weight into strength above $285. Do not add.\n\nCONVICTION: 9/15 (Medium).\nTARGET WEIGHT: 0% new; \u22643% existing. Kelly: 0% (negative edge).\n\nRE-ENTRY PLAN (if the long-term thesis remains intact):\n\u2022 Tranche 1 (1/2 position): at $240 \u2014 10% MoS to base IV; buy zone.\n\u2022 Tranche 2 (completion): at $210 \u2014 ~20% MoS to base IV, ~hand-over-fist vs bear\n  ($151).\n\u2022 Below $186 (52-wk low) \u2014 thesis re-evaluation, not automatic averaging.\n\u2022 Do not chase above $285; the bull case is already in the price.\n\nRATIONALE (numbers first):\n1. Probability-weighted intrinsic value is $220 vs price $292.26 \u2192 expected loss\n   of ~25% to convergence.\n2. Price is 2.5% ABOVE the bull-case IV of $285; even a perfect decade of execution\n   only justifies today's price.\n3. Multiples: 29.2x fwd P/E, 22.1x EV/EBITDA, 33.6x P/FCF, PEG 3.4 \u2014 all 20\u201335%\n   above history and above the quality-compounder norm.\n4. 3-year expected return is +4.9%/yr vs an 8.7% cost of equity \u2014 the market is\n   undercompensating the risk.\n5. This is a genuinel